<blockquote>
<p>I was just thinking the other day that there weren't any Mister Rogers skips, and now here we are and I'm sorry I asked. :(</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Apologies to Mr. Fred Rogers.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I thought the 'voices' part was incredibly silly, not to mention extremely helpful in explaining what was going on, which I never enjoy. It really threw me out of the article.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And that is fair. During the drafting phrase, it became apparent that not a lot of people are familiar with the muses of Greco-Roman myth and the voices served as a means of making the article more approachable to more readers. Admittedly it threw subtlety away, and it is quite silly, but then again Greco-Roman mythology can be quite the silly place. Such is life.</p>

